                <pb facs="0690" n="674" sameAs="frus:frus1947v08/pg674"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">822.00/9–1647: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Ecuador</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Simmons</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Quito</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1947-09-16">September 16,
                        1947</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>402. Congress elected Carlos Julio Arosemena Vice President by vote 103 to 3;
                    next session scheduled 4:30 p.m. Arosemena arrives Quito this afternoon.
                    Resignation Suarez expected to be acted upon immediately and Arosemena may be
                    installed as President today.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Simmons</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
